Configure the Costs Report
We cannot configure the CostAnalyzer as such. To show the results of the cost analysis, drag the
CostAnalyzer from the Frame onto the icon of the HtmlReport and drop it there.
• If the Content of the HtmlReport is inherited, the data of the CostAnalyzer 
  replaces the pre-defined
content of the HtmlReport. Plant Simulation opens the display window of the HtmlReport automatically.
Configure the Costs Report
Plant Simulation Help 10-423
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• If the Content of the HtmlReport is not inherited, Plant Simulation appends the data of the
CostAnalyzer to the pre-defined content of the HtmlReport. Plant Simulation opens the display window
of the HtmlReport automatically.
To show the results of the cost analysis, you can also drag the object CostAnalyzer into the open window
of the HtmlReport and drop it there, for example below the heading Statistics. Then the HtmlReport also
shows the pre-defined General Information when you click Show Report.
Configure the Costs Report
10-424 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

This adds the following instruction to the HtmlReport:
# Statistics
## CostAnalyzer
[CostAnalyzer]
Back to Simulate the Accrued Costs of the Machines
View the Costs Report
The HtmlReport shows the costs report with the settings we defined.
• In the table Investment Costs the Report shows the summed up investment costs of this Frame in the
unavailable cells.
Below it lists the investment costs, the depreciation period, and the operating costs of the individual
objects inserted into this Frame, row by row.
You can also query the investment costs with the method putInvestmentCostsIntoTable.
• In the table Piece Costs the Report shows die summed up piece costs of the used MU type, in our case
of the Part.
◦ The MU Type (part type) designates the name of the parts when they arrive in the Drain. When parts
change their name during the simulation, for example during the different production phases, the
costs are assigned to the final product.
View the Costs Report
Plant Simulation Help 10-425
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

◦ The Piece costs proper is the sum of the material costs, the accrued costs, and the general costs
are 8.32 €.
◦ The Material costs designate the costs, which accrue during the simulation when a new part enters
the production, are 8.00 €.
◦ The Accrued costs designate the costs, which are assigned to the part while it is processed on the
material flow object, are 0.17 €.
◦ The General costs designate the costs, which accrue when a material object is empty during the
simulation, are 0.15 €. These costs are distributed across the part types which were processed by the
material flow object.
◦ The Throughput designates the number of parts which were processed and moved through the
production line, 10650 parts in our case.
◦ The Work in process designates the number of parts which are currently passing through the
production process, 6 parts in our case.
Click Investment Costs in the dialog of the CostAnalyzer to show the investment costs.
You can also query the investment costs with the method putInvestmentCostsIntoTable.
Click Piece Costs in the dialog of the CostAnalyzer to show the piece costs.
You can also query the piece costs with the method putPieceCostsIntoTable.
Back to Simulate the Accrued Costs of the Machines
