Simulating the Power Consumption in Your Facility
Simulate the Power Consumption in Your Facility
To accommodate the growing environmental awareness, Plant Simulation provides features to keep track
of energy consumption in the face of rising energy costs and the depletion of energy resources.
The features on the Tab Energy provide these evaluations regarding energy consumption during the
production process in the plant:
• Power consumption per machine
• Total power consumption for all objects contained within a Frame
In our example we will demonstrate how to:
• Configure the Processing Stations and the Conveyor
• Configure the ShiftCalendar
• Check the Power Consumption in the Dialogs of the Objects
• Check the Power Consumption in the Statistics Report
• Check the Power Consumption in the Chart
We use most of the material flow objects with their default settings. We just entered energy-related
settings and defined failures for some of the objects.
The finished simulation model looks like this:
Simulating the Power Consumption in Your Facility
Plant Simulation Help 10-427
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Back to Modeling the Material Flow
Configure the Processing Stations and the Conveyor
Insert the following stations to simulate our parts moving through the factory.
• The Source feeds the parts into the plant. We did not change any of its default settings.
• The first machine, the Station, processes the parts for 1 minute each. We entered the kilowatts it uses
up in the states it can be in. We also entered the times that the machine requires for switching from one
energy state to another.
Configure the Processing Stations and the Conveyor
10-428 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• The second machine, Station1, processes the parts for 2 minutes each. We entered the kilowatts it uses
up in the states it can be in. We also entered the times that the machine requires for switching from one
energy state to another.
Configure the Processing Stations and the Conveyor
Plant Simulation Help 10-429
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To simulate a real situation, we also defined a failure profile with these settings:
Configure the Processing Stations and the Conveyor
10-430 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• The conveyor, the object of type Conveyor, transports the parts from the processing station Station1 to
the ParallelStation. We entered the kilowatts it uses up in the states it can be in. We also entered the
times that the conveyor requires for switching from one energy state to another. You will notice that the
length-oriented object Conveyor provides fewer energy settings than the point-oriented objects Station
and ParallelStation.
Configure the Processing Stations and the Conveyor
Plant Simulation Help 10-431
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To simulate a real situation, we also defined a failure profile with these settings:
• The third machine, the ParallelStation, processes the parts for 1 minute each. We entered the kilowatts
it uses up in the states it can be in. We also entered the times that the machine requires for switching
from one energy state to another.
Configure the Processing Stations and the Conveyor
10-432 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• The Drain removes the parts from the factory. We did not change any of its built-in settings.
• The Charts display a resource statistics chart, and an energy statistics chart for the selected objects.
Back to Simulate the Power Consumption in Your Facility
Configure the ShiftCalendar
To model a realistic situation in the factory, we insert a ShiftCalendar that controls the hours during which
people and machines work in the factory. We did not change the default shift times, we just entered the
material flow objects.
To do so, we held down Shift and dragged a marquee over the objects. We then dragged the selected
objects onto the ShiftCalendar 
  and dropped them there.
Configure the ShiftCalendar
Plant Simulation Help 10-433
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Back to Simulate the Power Consumption in Your Facility
Check the Power Consumption in the Dialogs of the Objects
You can view the energy consumption values, which the objects collected, in their dialogs.
• Double-click the icon of the respective object and click the Tab Statistics.
• Click Energy Statistics to view more detailed values about the different portions of energy
consumption.
Check the Power Consumption in the Dialogs of the Objects
10-434 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Back to Simulate the Power Consumption in Your Facility
Check the Power Consumption in the Statistics Report
You can check the power consumption of the material flow objects in you simulation model in the
StatisticsReport.
To view the total energy consumption and the portions of the different energy states, select Energy
Statistics in the drop-down list of the Statistics Report. The values are described under Energy Statistics
— Energy Statistics.
Check the Power Consumption in the Statistics Report
Plant Simulation Help 10-435
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
The energy states of the material flow objects differ from the resource states with the same name. The
values for the resource states refer to the statistics collection period, while the values for the energy
states refer to the total energy consumption.
The material flow objects also show these values on the Tab Statistics and in the dialog that clicking
Energy Statistics opens.
Back to Simulate the Power Consumption in Your Facility
Check the Power Consumption in the Chart
You can view the energy consumption values, which the objects collected, in a Chart.
• To view the energy consumption of the different energy states, select the objects which you want
to display in the Chart. Drag them onto the Chart. Select the Statistics Type > Energy Statistics in the
dialog that opens and click OK.
Check the Power Consumption in the Chart
10-436 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens